WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.262
NOT EXISTS asks whether no matching row can be found.

00:00:04.262 --> 00:00:08.532
For each patient, the inner query searches prescriptions.

00:00:08.532 --> 00:00:13.602
If there is no prescription with that patient ID, the patient is returned.

00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:19.812
This pattern appears everywhere: customers with no orders, students with no submissions,

00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:22.857
devices with no alerts, and patients with no prescription record.

00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:29.502
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:29.502 --> 00:00:35.102
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:35.102 --> 00:00:37.012
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:37.012 --> 00:00:42.872
In a real setting such as a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists,

00:00:42.872 --> 00:00:51.597
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:51.597 --> 00:00:53.862
before discussing syntax.

00:00:53.862 --> 00:01:00.240
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
